From d7cc5cb3ec5aa65bfd6542e4ed2345c8c9d3ad4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cli: show measured backhaul signal and contain hover cards

The topology already identifies the child's exact upstream AP BSSID, but it
does not expose the other endpoint of that wireless hop: the child's backhaul
STA.  Add that address to the normal Backhaul model and join it to associated
STA metrics reported by the parent AP.  Publish valid RCPI and derived RSSI on
the topology edge.  Values outside the EasyMesh RCPI range are omitted rather
than presented as signal.

Show that measured value in both extender and edge hovers.  Position topology
hover cards relative to their actual offset parent, flip them around the
cursor near an edge, and clamp them inside the topology viewport.  The old
page-relative calculation compared against viewport dimensions and could put
cards beyond the right or bottom edge.
---
